0.1 Definitions

For the purposes of this license:

"License" means this document.

"Toolchain", "Program" or "Covered Software" refers to the Wrench compiler, 
assembler, linker, driver, runtime environment, standard libraries, and 
associated utility software distributed under this License.

"Source Code" means the preferred form of the Toolchain for making modifications 
to it, including source files, header files, build scripts, and interface 
definition files.

"Contributor" means each individual or legal entity that creates, contributes 
to the creation of, or owns the Covered Software.

"Contribution" means Covered Software of a particular Contributor.

"Secondary License" means either the GNU General Public License, Version 2.0, 
the GNU Lesser General Public License, Version 2.1, the GNU Affero General 
Public License, Version 3.0, Mozilla Public License 2.0, or any later versions 
of those licenses.

"Modification" means any alteration, addition, or deletion made to existing 
files of the Toolchain’s Source Code, or any work containing portions of 
existing Toolchain files.

"Independent Work" or "Independent Module" means any separate source code file 
or module that does not contain, derive from, or modify existing files of the 
Toolchain, even if designed to interact or interoperate with the Toolchain.

"Generated Output" or "Output" refers to any executable, binary, object code, 
assembly text, or application data produced by running the Toolchain on 
user-supplied code, including any static or dynamic runtime library code 
embedded into or linked with such output.

"You" (or "Licensee") means an individual or legal entity exercising rights 
granted under this License.

0.2 Scope of Application

This License applies to any software component that contains a notice placed 
