SECTION 6: TERMINATION AND TWO-MONTH CURE PERIOD

6.1 Automatic Termination

The rights granted to You under this License will terminate automatically if 
You fail to comply with any of its terms or conditions (including file-level 
copyleft obligations under Section 2 or required commercial attributions under 
Section 3).

6.2 Two-Month Cure Period

Notwithstanding Section 6.1, Your rights under this License shall be 
provisionally reinstated if You cease all non-compliance, subject to the 
following rules:

    a) Self-Correction Upon Awareness: If You become aware of Your 
       non-compliance and fully remedy it prior to receiving formal notification, 
       Your rights under this License are fully restored.

    b) Formal Written Notice: If You receive a written notice of non-compliance 
       from the Licensor or an affected Contributor, You are granted a grace 
       period of two (2) calendar months from the date of receipt of such notice 
       to fully remedy and cure the non-compliance.

    c) Permanent Termination: If You fail to fully cure the non-compliance 
       within the two-month period following written notification (or two months 
       after becoming aware of the breach without taking corrective action), 
       all rights granted to You under this License shall be permanently 
       terminated without further notice.

6.3 Effect on Downstream Recipients

Termination of Your rights under this License shall not terminate, alter, or 
diminish the license rights of any third parties or end-users who received 
Generated Output, copies of Covered Software, or sublicenses from You in good 
faith prior to such termination, provided those third parties remain in full 
compliance with this License.


